"><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Aitken</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Falah</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning of <italic>Giardia lamblia</italic> heat shock protein HSP70 homologs: implications regarding origin of eukaryotic cells and of endoplasmic reticulum</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>1994</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>2895</fpage><lpage>2899</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8159675</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.91.8.2895</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roger</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Svard</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Tovar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillin</surname><given-names>FD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sogin</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A mitochondrial-like chaperonin 60 gene in <italic>Giardia lamblia</italic>: evidence that diplomonads once harbored an endosymbiont related to the progenitor of mitochondria</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>1998</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9419358</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.95.1.229</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keeling</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Burger</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Durnford</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><su